  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Better inclusion, greater rights: Promoting economic integration of the most disadvantaged groups of the City of Buenos Aires</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Low-income residents of irregular settlements of Buenos Aires face marginalization and isolation, which make it difficult for small businesses in these villas to be competitive. Asociacin Civil por la Igualdad y la Justicia (ACIJ) equips entrepreneurs with the skills and support necessary to facilitate their entry into the formal economy and overcome economic and social barriers. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions to expand economic opportunity in Argentina. ACIJ&apos;s activities encourage local entrepreneurship to ensure meaningful opportunities for communities to thrive.</narrative>
  </description>
